## Testing Guidelines

### Test types

| Type | Tool | DB / Redis |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Integration** | Supertest + Jest | Real Postgres test DB, real Redis |
| **Unit** | Jest | Mocked |

### Directory structure

```
src/tests/
  setup.js / teardown.js / setupFilesAfterEnv.js
  authentication/
    basic-login-controller.test.js
    basic-registration-controller.test.js
    logout-controller.test.js
    refresh-token-controller.test.js
  categories/
    create-category-controller.test.js
    list-categories-controller.test.js
    patch-category-controller.test.js
    delete-category-controller.test.js
```

Naming: `<action>-<resource>-controller.test.js`. Describe block: `describe('<METHOD> /v1/<resource>', () => { ... })`.

### User creation in tests

Use `faker` for collision-free data. Pass `passwordHash: 'irrelevant'` — the `beforeCreate` hook hashes it:

```js
const { faker } = require('@faker-js/faker');

user = await User.create({
    id: faker.string.uuid(),
    name: faker.person.fullName(),
    email: faker.internet.email(),
    passwordHash: 'irrelevant',
});
({ token: accessToken } = tokenService.signAccessToken({ sub: user.id, email: user.email }));
// Use as: `Authorization: Bearer ${accessToken}`
```

### Test case structure

```
describe('<METHOD> /v1/<resource>', () => {
    let user;
    let accessToken;

    beforeAll(async () => { /* Create user with faker, sign token */ });
    afterAll(async () => { /* Destroy child records first, then parent; { force: true } for paranoid */ });

    // 1. Authentication — missing header → 401
    // 2. Validation — missing/invalid field → 400
    // 3. Resource resolution — 404 not found; 403 wrong owner
    // 4. Business logic — 409 conflict (where applicable)
    // 5. Success — assert full serialized response shape
    // 6. Error propagation — direct controller call with empty req
});
```

#### Success assertion pattern

```js
expect(res.status).toBe(201);
expect(res.body).toHaveProperty('status', 'success');
expect(res.body.data).toMatchObject({ name: 'Side Projects', type: 'income', isDefault: false });
expect(res.body.data).toHaveProperty('categoryId');
expect(res.body.data).not.toHaveProperty('id');        // raw column not exposed
expect(res.body.data).not.toHaveProperty('deletedAt'); // paranoid field not exposed
```

#### Error propagation pattern

```js
it('should call next() with an error if any exception is thrown', async () => {
    req = {};
    res = { status: jest.fn().mockReturnThis(), json: jest.fn() };
    next = jest.fn();
    await createCategoryController(req, res, next);
    expect(next).toHaveBeenCalled();
});
```

### Determinism and isolation

- Delete child records before parent records (`Transaction` before `User`/`Category`).
- Use `{ force: true }` for paranoid models (`User`, `Category`).
- Scope all cleanup by `userId`. Never `truncate`.

### Coverage expectations

| Layer | Minimum tests |
| --- | --- |
| Authentication | Missing Authorization header |
| Validation | Missing + at least one invalid value per field |
| Resource resolution | 404 not found; 403 wrong owner |
| Business logic | At least one Conflict case (where applicable) |
| Success | One happy-path test asserting full serialized response shape |
| Error propagation | One direct controller call with empty `req` |

